# Turtle is compared byte-for-byte by the semantic baseline, so its line
# endings are part of the artifact. LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf decided the bytes: a Windows checkout produced
# CRLF, a Linux one LF, and 60 annotation triples across four files differed
# between them because a CRLF inside a multi-line literal is part of that
# literal value. The byte digests recorded before this rule describe the
# machine that measured them.
*.ttl text eol=lf
